  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Chasing Elena's taxi in a white horse-drawn carriage, Chef Barinov holds out the ring and asks her to marry him for real. Although Max and Vika's divorce is finalized the next day, Max believes a miracle is still possible—while Kostya role-plays as Masseur Konstantin for Nastya.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Отпусти меня!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Говорят, что мысли материальны.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Если признаться себе в том, чего по-настоящему хочешь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Возможно, чудо произойдёт.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Выходи за меня!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Теперь ваш брак официально расторгнут.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Но я не сдаюсь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Здравствуйте, можно заказать массаж?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Плюс интимные услуги?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Ну конечно можно!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Массажист Константин уже выезжает!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Жду вас с нетерпением!",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Отпусти меня!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Let me go!' The grammar packs 'let go' and 'me' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Говорят, что мысли материальны.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'They say that thoughts are material.' Max anchors the line on 'say', while 'material' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Если признаться себе в том, чего по-настоящему хочешь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'If you admit to yourself what you truly want.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'if' before landing on 'want'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Возможно, чудо произойдёт.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Perhaps a miracle will happen.' The meaning hinges on 'perhaps' working together with 'to happen' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Выходи за меня!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Marry me!' An emphatic spoken line centered on the verb meaning 'to go out'. Max answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Теперь ваш брак официально расторгнут.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Now your marriage is officially dissolved.' Max brings out the contrast between 'now' and 'your' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Но я не сдаюсь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'But I am not giving up.' Notice the reflexive suffix on the verb meaning 'to give up', turning the action back on the subject.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Здравствуйте, можно заказать массаж?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Hello, can I order a massage?' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'hello' and finishing on 'massage'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Плюс интимные услуги?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Plus intimate services?' Max anchors the line on 'plus', while 'services' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Ну конечно можно!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well of course you can!' Kostya anchors the line on 'come on', while 'may' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Массажист Константин уже выезжает!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Masseur Konstantin is already on his way!' Notice how Russian expresses 'massage therapist' and 'is heading out' with crisp inflection rather than helper words. Max answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Жду вас с нетерпением!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am waiting for you impatiently!' The meaning hinges on 'am waiting for' working together with 'impatience' in spoken Russian. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
